<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-elegans-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila elegans Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 1.8 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma), Pass 2 — MorphoEval overall 87.5/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 at 1.8 µm and 0 Ma. The Pass 1 nonlinear wavelength was 1.669 µm. Du was lengthened by the measured k ratio 1.08014. The FFT wavelength is now 1.799 µm. At the retuned Du, deflecta selects 2.372 µm and erecta 2.096 µm, both longer than the elegans linear mode (1.948 µm). A sweep of r/r_c from 1.02 to 3.20 at the uncorrected Du is monotonic (1.788 → 2.284 µm). Equal diffusion decays to std 1.4e-5 against a patterned std of 0.515 (KS 0.624). Seed CV of the nonlinear wavelength is 0.0023. The yellow-leaf mask gives foreground fraction 0.150, the largest red component has circularity 0.173, and the 159 px scale bar puts the non-leaf box at 3.55 mm by 2.15 mm. Dispersion Pearson r is 0.989, RMSE 0.031. Age 0 Ma, scale 1.8 µm. Overall 87.5/100 (faithfulness 87.3, reproducibility 87.9); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit dfaebd980203c4a087480f16a073f7fc0f6147bc; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 91, Morphological realism / specimen match 83, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 89, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 85, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_elegans_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-elegans-turing-wavelength-s0.py at dfaebd980203c4a087480f16a073f7fc0f6147bc, image/png, 485488 B, 1496×924 px, artifact_sha256 6c0b955363764bdc2c60c4d7d93334e1a8a9a4569fb5f1ea6cca096f04273ebd (sha256 6c0b955363764bdc2c60c4d7d93334e1a8a9a4569fb5f1ea6cca096f04273ebd), spec_fingerprint a12bb3100b597e414ef74972864fc5e5fa6a02a00d315c7492cd5f4151bd913e. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: a12bb3100b597e414ef74972864fc5e5fa6a02a00d315c7492cd5f4151bd913e; artifact_sha256: 6c0b955363764bdc2c60c4d7d93334e1a8a9a4569fb5f1ea6cca096f04273ebd; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_elegans_turing_wavelength_s0/README.md=92b2e690554d6b38..., datasets/drosophila_elegans_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_elegans_specimen.jpg=ed8dfe6c85be35e1..., datasets/drosophila_elegans_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_elegans_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=e5d4cbec3c5231fc..., datasets/drosophila_elegans_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=f3905fa5ed82ba4a..., datasets/drosophila_elegans_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=98aa35f7c02c324d...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-drosophila-elegans-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Yeh, Liou & True 2006: male D. elegans has an apical wing melanin patch used in courtship, divergent from D. gunungcola. | Turing 1952 dispersion relation and Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics.; reconstructed_in_script: NONLINEAR_K_CORRECTION = 1.08014 is the Pass 1 ratio of linear to nonlinear wavelength, used to re-solve Du. | Deflecta 2.372 µm and erecta 2.096 µm are the same law at r/r_c = 2.65 and 1.48 with that Du.; transfer_boundary: Deflecta and erecta are chronoseries neighbors, not the gunungcola comparison in Yeh and Massey.; does_not_claim: The photograph does not resolve 1.8 µm granules. The lattice is the simulated field, shown magnified. | Eye circularity 0.173 is the largest red component, not a claim that one ommatidial field is a circle. | The 3.55 mm box includes wings and legs; it is not a new measurement of thorax length. | No second assessor scored this pass. Nanopubs were not signed.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.75e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-elegans-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila elegans Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 1.8 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma), Pass 2 — Parameter expressivity: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "At fixed activator diffusivity, raising r/r_c from 1.02 to 3.20 lengthens the linear wavelength monotonically from 1.788 µm to 2.284 µm. The equal-diffusion control (Du = Dv) falls to std 1.4e-5 while the elegans pattern holds std 0.515. Both controls do what the dispersion law says they should." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-elegans-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-elegans-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

