<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-elegans-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila elegans Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 1.8 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma), Pass 2 — Morphological realism / specimen match: 83/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The comparison still sets the real adult beside a hexagonal activator lattice, and the 12-frame GIF ends on the photograph. Pass 2 adds a leaf mask that actually separates the yellow leaf (foreground 0.150) and reports the red eye and the 1 mm bar. The lattice remains a magnified subcellular field: this macro photograph cannot show 1.8 µm granules, so the match is phenotypic context plus pattern class, not a pixel identity of the ocellus texture." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-elegans-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-elegans-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-elegans-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.3e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-elegans-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila elegans Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 1.8 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma), Pass 2 (Drosophila elegans)",
        "Drosophila elegans Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 1.8 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma), Pass 2 faithfully reproduces Drosophila elegans morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-elegans-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-elegans-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-elegans-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-elegans-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila elegans specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-elegans-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Drosophila elegans" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Eye circularity 0.173 is the largest red component, not a claim that one ommatidial field is a circle.",
        "does_not_claim: No second assessor scored this pass. Nanopubs were not signed.",
        "does_not_claim: The 3.55 mm box includes wings and legs; it is not a new measurement of thorax length.",
        "does_not_claim: The photograph does not resolve 1.8 µm granules. The lattice is the simulated field, shown magnified.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Deflecta 2.372 µm and erecta 2.096 µm are the same law at r/r_c = 2.65 and 1.48 with that Du.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: NONLINEAR_K_CORRECTION = 1.08014 is the Pass 1 ratio of linear to nonlinear wavelength, used to re-solve Du.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation and Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics.",
        "reported_in_source: Yeh, Liou & True 2006: male D. elegans has an apical wing melanin patch used in courtship, divergent from D. gunungcola.",
        "transfer_boundary: Deflecta and erecta are chronoseries neighbors, not the gunungcola comparison in Yeh and Massey." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Drosophila elegans (Morning-Glory Flower-Breeding Fly)" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Drosophila" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-elegans-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/drosophila_elegans_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Drosophila elegans; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Yeh, Liou & True 2006: male D. elegans has an apical wing melanin patch used in courtship, divergent from D. gunungcola. | Turing 1952 dispersion relation and Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics.; reconstructed_in_script: NONLINEAR_K_CORRECTION = 1.08014 is the Pass 1 ratio of linear to nonlinear wavelength, used to re-solve Du. | Deflecta 2.372 µm and erecta 2.096 µm are the same law at r/r_c = 2.65 and 1.48 with that Du.; transfer_boundary: Deflecta and erecta are chronoseries neighbors, not the gunungcola comparison in Yeh and Massey.; does_not_claim: The photograph does not resolve 1.8 µm granules. The lattice is the simulated field, shown magnified. | Eye circularity 0.173 is the largest red component, not a claim that one ommatidial field is a circle. | The 3.55 mm box includes wings and legs; it is not a new measurement of thorax length. | No second assessor scored this pass. Nanopubs were not signed.]; phenomenon_size: 1.9 µm (1.919e-06 m, log10=-5.717 m, tier=3_subcellular_um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 1.9 µm to 4.3 mm): 1.9 µm:drosophila-affinis-bioelectric-polarity, 6.0 µm:drosophila-affinis-vertex-packing, 96 µm:drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength, 192 µm:drosophila-affinis-clock-wavefront, 432 µm:drosophila-affinis-morphogen-condensation, 528 µm:drosophila-affinis-elastic-buckling, 600 µm:drosophila-affinis-flux-canalization, 840 µm:drosophila-affinis-branching-tree" ;
